{
  "id": "open-ward",
  "term": "open ward",
  "definition": "An open ward is a psychiatric hospital ward that is managed with open doors rather than as a locked unit, including for some involuntarily committed patients where legally permitted. In this context, it refers to a least-restrictive approach to inpatient care that relies on ward organization, staff presence, and other measures instead of routine locking.",
